I understand this must be a difficult time for you. I'm really sorry to hear about the changes happening with your role. It's natural to feel uncertain or anxious during times like these. Let's focus on how we can best support each other through this transition.

Firstly, let me know if there’s anything specific you need right from my side – whether it’s help finding new opportunities within the company, advice on updating your resume, or simply someone to talk things over with. 

If you're open to it, maybe we could discuss some next steps together? We can explore any internal transfer options that might still up. Or perhaps brainstorm ways you could leverage your skills elsewhere in the organization. 

In the meantime, take yourself. Take care of your mental health by reaching out to friends and family too. If you decide to look for work outside the company, I'd be happy to connect you with recruiters who specialize in helping people find jobs after corporate restructurings.

Remember, while this may seem scary now, many people have successfully navigate such transitions and come out stronger on the other side. You've got experience and abilities that will serve you well moving forward.

