### PASS A: VANILLA ###

In the heart of the stormy coast stood Lighthouse Point, its beam piercing the night. Among its keepers was young Eli, an apprentice with a secret fear—of the dark. Each evening, as he climbed to the top, his hands trembled. One stormy night, a fierce gale threatened to extinguish the light. With trembling steps, Eli ascended alone. As thunder roared, he clung to the ladder, eyes wide in terror. But then, a soft voice whispered, "Fear not, for I am here.” It was the lighthouse cat, always by his side. Together, they reached the top just in time. The beam flickered back on, banishing shadows. Eli realized that courage wasn’t fearless; it was facing your fears. From that day forward, he faced each night with newfound bravery.

