Firstly, know that it’s okay to process these feelings in whatever way feels right for you—whether that means talking with someone, writing down how you’re feeling, or finding other activities that help you relax and take yourself.

It might also be beneficial to talk things over with an adult who understands family law or has experience dealing with similar situations. They could provide some clarity on why certain decisions were made and offer you on moving forward.

Remember, while this may not change today’s reality, there are still steps you can take towards improving your situation in the future. Sometimes, even if we don’t like everything as planned, life finds ways to bring us closer together and teach us valuable lessons along the way.

Lastly, try to stay positive and focus on the support system around you. You have people who care about you deeply and want to see you through this tough time.

